      "physical_description": null,
      "summary": "Alabastron. Long tapering body, flat rounded lip; the upper part is in the form of a woman (goddess?), the head covered by a long wig, from which rises the mouth of the vase. The eyes are large and oblique, the upper lid angular; the nose is aquiline (the point abraded); the lips are delicately worked and slightly curved; the chin is pointed; the right cheek is split away; the ears are merely blocked out. The neck is long. The right hand held a lotos flower between the breasts; the left arm hung at the side, the fingers clenched, holding an object. The left side is much injured by weathering and most of the arm above the wrist, which is sleeved, is missing. The right breast is also injured. The modelling of the right arm is of advanced style.\r\nWhite alabaster.",
      "historical_context": null,
      "dimensions": [],
